  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-17T04:46:50.564Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's nice to finally have very specific details on what standards VRchat expects from avatar creators for both public worlds and personal avatars.\n\nIs there any way we could get a detailed write-up on exactly how each avatar component affects performance and a roadmap on how VRchat plans to optimize over time to account for the various components?\n\nOr more plainly.  How much does things like dynamic bones and colliders actually affect performance in a numeric scale.  Are we talking dozens of FPS loss, just a few?  Is this all towards the ability to exist in a world with hundreds of avatars someday?\n\nI have a mid-to-high end system and even with VRchat's grey robots in an un-optimized world (dynamic lighting, etc), I get pretty severe FPS drops.\n\nOn that point as well, when are more stringent standards going to be set for worlds with always-on mirrors and dynamic lighting with shadows, which have always had a much larger impact on FPS than any amount of dynamic bones and colliders?\n\nOnce again, very appreciative that we are finally getting some solid standards and guidelines of what VRchat expects from us as avatar creators.  Would just love more technical info and a better idea of the road forward in terms of what VRchat is doing to optimize the base game.",
